{"cuisine/udmurt-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/udmurt-cuisine","n":"Udmurt cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Russia","intro":[["Udmurt cuisine consists of the cuisine of Udmurtia and the Udmurt people, and is characterized by the rich use of local foods. Old traditions include foods made from grains and flour, especially milled rye, barley, wheat, and buckwheat. Meat, vegetables and black bread are staple foods in Udmurt cuisine. Additional foods include pelmeni, pancakes, pastries and small tarts. Milk is a scarce commodity, and that which exists is often made into ayran, a type of sour milk."],["The Udmurt people have historically been involved in cattle breeding, agricultural production and hunting. Beekeeping is a common practice among the Udmurts and other groups in the area, and pig farming also exists. Potatoes, vegetables and flax are produced in significant quantities in Udmurtia. For total agricultural production in Russia, Udmurtia was ranked as 33rd."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"udmurt-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Udmurt_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/cuisine-of-abruzzo":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-abruzzo","n":"Abruzzese and Molisan cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Italy","intro":[["Cuisine of Abruzzo is eclectic, drawing on pastoral, mountain, and coastal cuisine. Staples of Abruzzo cuisine include bread, pasta, meat, fish, cheese, and wine. The isolation which has characterized the region for centuries has ensured the independence of its culinary tradition from those of nearby regions. Local cuisine was widely appreciated in a 2013 survey among foreign tourists."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-abruzzo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_Abruzzo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":10,"links":[["Arrosticini","dish/arrosticini"],["Aurum (liqueur)","dish/aurum-liqueur"],["Brodetto alla vastese","dish/brodetto-alla-vastese"],["Centerbe","dish/centerbe"],["Confetti di Sulmona","dish/confetti-di-sulmona"],["Fiadone","dish/fiadone"],["Mortadella di Campotosto","dish/mortadella-di-campotosto"],["Pecora alla callara","dish/pecora-alla-callara"],["Torrone Nurzia","dish/torrone-nurzia"],["Vino cotto","dish/vino-cotto"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Great Italian Chefs: Abruzzese recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatitalianchefs.com","note":"Collection of dishes from Abruzzo by Italian chefs on an established recipe site.","url":"https://www.greatitalianchefs.com/collections/abruzzese-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"The Pasta Project: Abruzzo","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"the-pasta-project.com","note":"Italy-based pasta blog's section on regional pasta dishes from Abruzzo.","url":"https://www.the-pasta-project.com/abruzzo/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/d/d8/Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg/500px-Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg","w":500,"h":668,"by":"Ra Boe","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg","of":"Arrosticini"}},"dish/batatas-a-murro":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/batatas-a-murro","n":"Batatas a murro","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Portuguese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Batatas a murro is a Portuguese recipe and cooking technique using new potatoes that are lightly smashed."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-batatas-a-murro"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batatas_a_murro"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Food From Portugal","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"foodfromportugal.com","note":"Portuguese-run recipe site and video channel of traditional Portuguese dishes.","url":"https://www.foodfromportugal.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Portuguese cuisine","links":[["Alheira","dish/alheira"],["Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","dish/ameijoas-a-bulhao-pato"],["Arroz de marisco","dish/arroz-de-marisco"],["Bacalhau à Brás","dish/bacalhau-a-bras"],["Bacalhau à Gomes de Sá","dish/bacalhau-a-gomes-de-sa"],["Bacalhau à minhota","dish/bacalhau-a-minhota"],["Bacalhau à Narcisa","dish/bacalhau-a-narcisa"],["Bacalhau à Zé do Pipo","dish/bacalhau-a-ze-do-pipo"],["Bacalhau com natas","dish/bacalhau-com-natas"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bolo de bolacha","dish/bolo-de-bolacha"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Encharcada","dish/encharcada"],["Fartura","dish/fartura"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Fios de ovos","dish/fios-de-ovos"],["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Pão Alentejano","dish/pao-alentejano"],["Pão de Ló","dish/pao-de-lo"],["Pataniscas","dish/pataniscas"],["Polvo à lagareiro","dish/polvo-a-lagareiro"],["Prego (Portuguese sandwich)","dish/prego-portuguese-sandwich"],["Pudim Abade de Priscos","dish/pudim-abade-de-priscos"],["Pudim Molotov","dish/pudim-molotov"],["Sericaia","dish/sericaia"],["Serradura","dish/serradura"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/8/84/Espinho%2C_Portugal_%2849659059181%29.jpg/500px-Espinho%2C_Portugal_%2849659059181%29.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"brazilian.wanderluster from RIO DE JANEIRO, Brasil - Brazil","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Espinho%2C_Portugal_(49659059181).jpg"}},"ingredient/capparis":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/capparis","n":"Capparis","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Capparis is a genus of flowering plants in the family Capparaceae. It includes about 140 species of shrubs or lianas which are collectively known as caper shrubs or caperbushes. Capparis species occur over a wide range of habitat in the subtropical and tropical regions of Africa, Eurasia, Australasia, and the Pacific."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-capparis"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capparis"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Biff à la Lindström","dish/biff-a-la-lindstrom"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Beta vulgaris","ingredient/beta-vulgaris"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/8/82/Starr_050223-4262_Capparis_sandwichiana.jpg/500px-Starr_050223-4262_Capparis_sandwichiana.jpg","w":500,"h":374,"by":"Forest & Kim Starr","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Starr_050223-4262_Capparis_sandwichiana.jpg"}},"ingredient/aspergillus-tubingensis":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/aspergillus-tubingensis","n":"Aspergillus tubingensis","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Aspergillus tubingensis is a darkly pigmented species of fungus in the genus Aspergillus section Nigri. It is often confused with Aspergillus niger due to their similar morphology and habitat. A. tubingensis is often involved in food spoilage of fruits and wheat, and industrial fermentation. This species is a rare agent of opportunistic infection."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-aspergillus-tubingensis"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aspergillus_tubingensis"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Kōji (food)","dish/koji-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Aspergillus luchuensis","ingredient/aspergillus-luchuensis"],["Aspergillus niger","ingredient/aspergillus-niger"],["Aspergillus oryzae","ingredient/aspergillus-oryzae"],["Aspergillus sojae","ingredient/aspergillus-sojae"],["Aspergillus tamarii","ingredient/aspergillus-tamarii"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/2a/Aspergillus_tubingensis_FJBJ11.png/500px-Aspergillus_tubingensis_FJBJ11.png","w":500,"h":399,"by":"Qing-Wei Tan, Fang-Luan Gao, Fu-Rong Wang, and Qi-Jian Chen","lic":"CC BY 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aspergillus_tubingensis_FJBJ11.png"}},"dish/quesabirria":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/quesabirria","n":"Quesabirria","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Quesabirria ('cheese birria') (also called birria tacos or red tacos) is a Mexican dish comprising birria-style cooked beef folded into a tortilla with melted cheese and served with a side of broth (Spanish: consomé) for dipping. The dish has origins in Tijuana, Mexico, where it was originally made with goat meat, and gained popularity in the United States through Instagram. It is now made also with other meats, such as beef and chicken."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-quesabirria"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quesabirria"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Consommé","ingredient/consomme"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pati Jinich","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Chile con queso","dish/chile-con-queso"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Concha","dish/concha"],["Discada","dish/discada"],["El Adobe de Capistrano","dish/el-adobe-de-capistrano"],["Guacamole","dish/guacamole"],["Huevos rancheros","dish/huevos-rancheros"],["List of Mexican restaurants","dish/list-of-mexican-restaurants"],["Mexican juice bar","dish/mexican-juice-bar"],["Mexican restaurant","dish/mexican-restaurant"],["Nachos","dish/nachos"],["Pico de gallo","dish/pico-de-gallo"],["Pozole","dish/pozole"],["Quesadilla","dish/quesadilla"],["Real Mex Restaurants","dish/real-mex-restaurants"],["Relleno negro","dish/relleno-negro"],["Sopa de lima","dish/sopa-de-lima"],["Taco","dish/taco"],["Taquería","dish/taqueria"],["Tortilla soup","dish/tortilla-soup"],["Walnut soup","dish/walnut-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/8/8c/Quesabirria_at_Taqueria_La_Hacienda%2C_Sonoma%2C_California_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/500px-Quesabirria_at_Taqueria_La_Hacienda%2C_Sonoma%2C_California_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg","w":500,"h":389,"by":"Missvain","lic":"CC BY 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quesabirria_at_Taqueria_La_Hacienda%2C_Sonoma%2C_California_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg"}},"ingredient/frog-leg":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/frog-leg","n":"Frog leg","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Frog legs are the muscular hindlimbs of frogs that are consumed as food by humans in some cuisines. Frog legs are rich in protein, omega-3 fatty acids, vitamin A, and potassium. They are often said to taste like chicken because of the mild flavor, with a texture most similar to chicken wings. The taste and texture of frog meat are approximately between chicken and fish. Frog muscles do not resolve rigor mortis as quickly as skeletal muscles from warm-blooded animals (chicken, for example) do, so heat from cooking can cause fresh frog legs to twitch when in the pan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-frog-leg"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frog_leg"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Swikee","dish/swikee"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Frog legs","ingredient/frog-legs"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/e4/2012_Froschschenkel_anagoria.JPG/500px-2012_Froschschenkel_anagoria.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Anagoria","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2012_Froschschenkel_anagoria.JPG"}},"ingredient/vodka":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/vodka","n":"Vodka","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Vodka is a clear distilled alcoholic beverage. Its varieties originated in Poland and Russia. Vodka is composed mainly of water and ethanol (alcohol), sometimes with traces of impurities and flavourings. Traditionally it is made by distilling liquid from fermented cereal grains and potatoes since the latter was introduced in Europe in the 18th century. Some modern brands use maize, sugar cane, fruit, honey, or maple sap as the base."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-vodka"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vodka"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine",[["Vodka sauce","dish/vodka-sauce"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Crushed red pepper","ingredient/crushed-red-pepper"],["Pancetta","ingredient/pancetta"],["Penne","ingredient/penne"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/d/de/Smirnoff_Red_Label_8213.jpg/500px-Smirnoff_Red_Label_8213.jpg","w":500,"h":750,"by":"Ashley Pomeroy","lic":"CC BY 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smirnoff_Red_Label_8213.jpg"}}}